---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const parts = [
  {
    id: 'core',
    eyebrow: 'One core',
    title: 'Two front doors, one set of commands.',
    body: [
      'Every command is defined once: its inputs, whether it writes, and its examples. The same definition is exposed as a CLI command and as an MCP tool, and both run exactly the same code.',
      'A test walks every command and proves the two front doors accept the same inputs, send the same requests and return the same result, so they cannot drift apart.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'output',
    eyebrow: 'Output',
    title: 'One JSON envelope, every time.',
    body: [
      'Every command prints exactly one envelope: ok, data, error and meta. Errors carry a stable code and a fix you can act on, never a stack trace. A mistyped command gets an envelope too, so an agent never has to read help text to learn it typed something wrong.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'configuration',
    eyebrow: 'Configuration',
    title: 'Your environment, then your config.',
    body: [
      'Settings come from TOIL_* environment variables first, then your own config in your home folder. Pipelines and agents configure toil without editing a file.',
      'Nothing inside a repository can change where your credentials go or switch on writes. Knowledge about a body of work, such as its repositories, issue keys and environments, is planned to live in dossiers: your own files, with no hosts and no secrets, that name connections you set up yourself.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'credentials',
    eyebrow: 'Credentials',
    title: 'One token, pasted once, kept safe.',
    body: [
      'Every integration signs in with a long-lived token you generate once in the service itself. There are no browser logins, no OAuth pop-ups and no device codes.',
      "Tokens come from environment variables first, which is how CI provides them, then from your toil config. You can keep them in your operating system's credential store instead, with only a reference in config, but nothing requires it. Tokens never appear on a command line or in output.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'safety',
    eyebrow: 'Safety',
    title: 'Reads are free. Writes need two yeses.',
    body: [
      'Anything that changes data needs writes switched on for that service in your own config, and --allow-write on the call. Over MCP, write tools are not even listed until writes are on.',
      '--verbose lists every request a command made, with credentials removed, so you can see exactly what it touched.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'mcp',
    eyebrow: 'MCP',
    title: 'A stand-in for servers you can’t install.',
    body: [
      'toil mcp serves over stdio and never opens a network port. Scope it with --areas to give an agent a small, focused set of tools, standing in for vendor MCP servers that are blocked or need a browser login.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'install',
    eyebrow: 'Install',
    title: 'Nothing for application control to block.',
    body: [
      'toil is a single JavaScript file on the Node you already have: no executable, no native module and no install script. Every build is checked to import only Node’s own modules and to contain only the files it should.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<Layout title="How it works" description="How toil works at a high level: one core behind the CLI and MCP, the JSON envelope, configuration, credentials, write safety and installation.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="How it works"
    title="The big picture, <em>briefly.</em>"
    lead="What toil is made of and the promises it keeps. For specifics, such as setup steps, configuration keys and each integration, see the docs."
  />

  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="prerelease" data-reveal>
        <strong>Pre-release.</strong> The core described here is built and tested, but no integration has shipped and nothing is on npm
        yet. Dossiers are still a design.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="container hiw">
      <nav class="hiw__toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <p class="eyebrow">On this page</p>
        <ul>
          {parts.map((p) => <li><a class="tap" href={`#${p.id}`}>{p.eyebrow}</a></li>)}
        </ul>
      </nav>
      <div class="hiw__parts">
        {parts.map((p, n) => (
          <section class="hiw__part" id={p.id} data-reveal>
            <span class="hiw__n">{String(n + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">{p.eyebrow}</p>
              <h2>{p.title}</h2>
              {p.body.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
            </div>
          </section>
        ))}
        <p class="more" data-reveal><a class="tap" href={url('/docs/')}>Read the detailed docs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hiw { display: grid; gap: var(--space-lg); padding-block: var(--space-lg); }
  .hiw > * { min-width: 0; }

  .hiw__toc ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0 1.2rem; margin-top: var(--space-2xs); }
  .hiw__toc a { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .hiw__toc a:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }

  .hiw__parts { display: grid; gap: var(--space-xl); }
  .hiw__part { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: var(--space-md); scroll-margin-top: 88px; }
  .hiw__part > * { min-width: 0; }
  .hiw__n { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-3xl); line-height: 1; color: transparent; -webkit-text-stroke: 1px var(--color-accent); }
  .hiw__part h2 { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin: var(--space-2xs) 0 var(--space-xs); }
  .hiw__part p:not(.eyebrow) { color: var(--color-muted); max-width: 62ch; }
  .hiw__part p + p { margin-top: var(--space-xs); }

  .more a { color: var(--color-accent); font-family: var(--font-action); font-weight: 500; }

  .prerelease { border: 1px solid var(--color-accent); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md); color: var(--color-muted); max-width: 62ch; }
  .prerelease strong { color: var(--color-accent); }

  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .hiw { grid-template-columns: 12rem minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; }
    .hiw__toc { position: sticky; top: 88px; }
    .hiw__toc ul { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
